==Trivia==
*Grotesque Gallery's Japanese name, Henrankai no E (変覧会の絵), is a reference to ''Tenrankai no E'' (展覧会の絵), the Japanese name of [[wikipedia:Modest Mussorgsky|Modest Mussorgsky]]'s famous piano suite '' [[wikipedia:Pictures at an Exhibition|Pictures at an Exhibition]]''. ''Henrankai'' (変覧会) is not an actual word, but a pun on ''tenrankai'' (展覧会, exhibition) with the first kanji replaced by 変 (change; strange/odd).
*All the stages are named after a type of an art technique or movement.

